# Audio runtime guard patch status

This patch file was originally added as a planning artifact.

The audio hardening work has now been applied directly to:

```text
sc0710-audio.c
```

Do not apply this file with `git am`.

## Applied direction

The applied code now:

- Tracks whether ALSA capture is actively running.
- Silently ignores DMA audio delivery when no PCM capture stream is active.
- Avoids noisy kernel log spam for inactive, missing, or not yet prepared PCM runtime state.
- Tracks ALSA period boundaries before calling `snd_pcm_period_elapsed()`.
- Uses `vzalloc()` and `vfree()` for the PCM DMA area so the existing `.page` callback can use `vmalloc_to_page()` safely.
- Resets capture state on close, hardware free, stop, suspend, and pause.

## Why this is a note instead of a patch now

The original patch proposal modified `sc0710.h`. The applied implementation keeps the public audio device structure unchanged and stores the new capture state in `sc0710-audio.c` static per-board arrays. That keeps the audio patch smaller while the larger videobuf2 port is still pending.
